# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# These keep inbound links working. next.config.ts cannot do this job because
# `redirects()` needs a server and this site is a static export.
#
# Format: <from>  <to>  <status>.  :placeholder matches one segment, * matches
# the rest of the path. First match wins, so order matters.

# November 2026: project pages moved from /work/<slug>/ to /projects/<slug>/,
# and /work/ became the work-experience page.
#
# One line per project, never a /work/:slug or /work/* placeholder. Cloudflare
# applies redirects before it serves files, and the Work page has its own files
# under /work/ (index.txt and the __next.*.txt data the site loads when you
# click a link to /work/). A placeholder caught those and sent every click on a
# Work link to a 404 (fixed November 10). npm run validate fails on a
# placeholder rule here. A project added after November 2026 never had a
# /work/ address, so it needs no line.
